# Copy to .env and adjust. .env is git-ignored.

# --- limits (apply to both usecases) ---
SBX_MEMORY=4g
SBX_CPUS=2
# Wrapper fallback when unset here: 1024 (code), 2048 (pentest — nmap &
# parallel scanners fork many threads). A value set here always wins.
SBX_PIDS=1024

# --- model backend ---
# The sandbox reuses the host's Claude Code model config, so there is nothing
# to duplicate here: same model, effort, context and key, with only the
# loopback base URL rewritten to host.containers.internal (the runtime's
# pasta host address). The port is parsed from the base URL and granted to
# the proxy as a trusted upstream automatically. To use the real Anthropic
# API, change the host config (or point SBX_CLAUDE_CONFIG elsewhere / unset
# it and set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY).
# SBX_CLAUDE_CONFIG=$HOME/claude.sh

# --- network egress ---
# 1 = open egress (proxy logs everything but bypasses the allowlist),
# 0 = allowlist enforced. Wrapper defaults: code=1 (open), pentest=0.
# A value set here always wins over the wrapper default.
# SBX_OPEN_NETWORK=1
